 "strings": {
  "Tom is a foreigner who admires the samurai. If I've got the time, maybe I can go to the Sengoku residence to train him.": "",
  "Me, play house? Uh... I've never done that. I didn't even do it back when I was a kid.": "",
  "Hate to think it, but maybe Fujie's proposal would have been accepted if I'd just been better at teaching him the Tosa dialect.": "",
  "Kanda, the artist to be entertained, is at Watami... Guess it would be a good deed to help the okami.": "",
  "I got lured into ee ja nai ka, and what a truly terrible dance it is. Now I need to get everything calmed down.": "",
  "My precious, precious inari sushi... I didn't get to eat it! But... I suppose it's better that it went to a sick child.": "",
  "I may have caused the whole thing in the first place, but at least I was able to save a family. Thank goodness.": "",
  "My carelessness caused two men to take each others' packages. One said he was heading to Mukurogai...": "",
  "I heard a scream from the room next to mine. What in the world is going on?": "",
  "The Kuramitsu family servant asked me to protect the palanquin. Someone named Hayakaze is threatening the Kuramitsu daughter.": "",
  "The man on the ground turned out to be a sumo wrestler. I had to give him some of my food, but at least I was able to pass...": "",
  "Yae the debt collector, huh? She's not a bad person, but I bet she has lots of enemies because of her work. I should help her out sometime.": "",
  "I healed the injured man, and apparently he's the type to personally help people in need. I really admire that guy.": "",
  "Maybe that dog was lethargic because it was hungry. I should bring it something to eat.": "",
  "Yae said she had some work for me. I should go see her at Kurogane Smithing and see what she's got in mind.": "",
  "The plan is to go to the gambling den to help out one of Yae's regulars. First step is to meet Yae at Kurogane Smithing.": "",
  "Y'know, maybe it wasn't me who motivated Uchitaro to get out and about. Maybe it was his love for his mother and hers for him.": "",
  "The Sword Nut (Beginning)": "",
  "When even the sword-collector compliments your blade, you know you've got a good one. And he even wants to see my weapon again...": "",
  "When she saw Takeda lose, Hirakawa was released from the curse. But I'm sure a new \"Kyo's Fastest\" will be anointed any day now...": "",
  "It was a risky bet, but Uchitaro finally came out of the house to protect his mother. Now to take care of these guys...": "",
  "I hope my response reaches the diary owner, who seems to have it bad for some guy. Hey, why not visit the Kamo River Shrine again?": "",
  "I could go to South Yashikimachi again, if I ever muster up the courage to listen to Sakiko again...": "",
  "The okami of Shikokuya wanted help entertaining a famous artist. But it was just too big a request...": "",
  "That courier who injured his leg on the Shijo Bridge was so pathetic he was annoying. But... is it possible he's still waiting for someone to help him?": "",
  "Fujie's having trouble reading a letter written in a Tosa dialect, and could really use some help. He's somewhere near Ikedaya.": "",
  "There was a teacher at a private school who didn't know how to explain a globe to his students. Hope he figured it out...": "",
  "I don't want to bother Natsumi. I'll avoid going to his room for a while.": "",
  "I don't want to interrupt Natsumi if he's working. I won't go to his room quite yet.": "",
  "I respect that foreign guy, Creek. But I hope he doesn't get himself in yet another dangerous situation.": "",
  "All in the Hips (Beginning)": "",
  "Were those two really the ones who ate the mochi...?": "",
  "I met a strange boy who actually likes vegetables...": "",
  "There was a woman trying to get to Mukurogai from the docks east of Teradaya. It sounds pretty dangerous... Maybe I should help her.": "",
  "I gave the boy something I didn't want, and I think he actually really liked it. I don't understand kids...": "",
  "I promised the boy I'd give him something. I don't know what kids like these days, but I could take a look at what I have and don't want.": "",
  "A foreigner is getting pretty rowdy at the izakaya. Hopefully he's not giving the local riffraff any ideas...": "",
  "If the Shinsengumi see me playing house in front of the barracks... Oh, it's too awful to imagine. I can't do it, even for the children.": "",
  "A bear near the barracks? It's hard to believe, but if it's real, nothing could be more dangerous. I need to take that boy's story seriously.": "",
  "I took the injured old lady home, and her tea was delicious!": "",
  "I helped the dog with its wounds, but it'll be some time before it's fully recovered. I probably need to give it regular treatment.": "",
  "There was a stray dog who was hurt... possibly pretty badly. I should get something to treat its injuries.": "",
  "So the diary owner is finally going to confess her love. I hope it works out. She's probably going to do it right at Kamo River Shrine in Gion...": "",
  "I wrote a response to the diary owner, who clearly has a more optimistic view of romance than I do. I think I'll visit the shrine again.": "",
  "This is unforgivable—a con artist pretending to be Ebisu-sama and stealing money from our elders. Hopefully, some of the people on Shijo Street can serve as witnesses.": "",
  "Love Beyond Borders (Beginning)": "",
  "I may have gotten roped into it, but I did share drinks with him. I won't let this guy cut Satow down so easily.": "",
  "I delivered my meal to the chef. Supposedly he's about to make a big culinary breakthrough...": "",
  "Satow has deep respect for Japan, and I'm going to help him with his research by searching for memoirs and bringing them to the izakaya.": "",
  "There's a chef who's on a mission to change Japan. I promised to bring him some meals made by my own hand.": "",
  "Maybe it's time for Japan to learn about the outside world and all the other nations of the world...": "",
  "Satow was thinking of Japan, even more so than the Japanese people. It's his passion. I'll stick around a bit, to see his dream realized.": "",
  "I made the diary owner angry... But she asked how I felt and I gave my honest answer. I should just leave this thing alone.": "",
  "A man named Akechi asked me to make some food for a warlord. He's waiting at Hanako, an izakaya in Fushimi. I ought to head over there...": "",
  "I made food for this warlord, Okehazama. Obviously, that rumor about him killing people who served him bad food was a total lie.": "",
  "Some sad excuse of a son actually made his own mother cry during an argument in East Umekojicho. What could've caused him to do that?": "",
  "There was a hungry cat in East Umekojicho. I bet it'd start purring fast if I gave it some fish...": "",
  "Using your power to abuse the poor... Truly, this man is unworthy of the title of samurai. He is lower than a dog—and he needs an obedience lesson from me.": "",
  "The Spitfire Town Protector (Beginning)": "",
  "These men are not worthy of being samurai. Tom, show them what a real samurai is.": "",
  "I lost the race with Takeda. But it can't end here. If he's near Teradaya, I'm going to settle the score with him...": "",
  "The Filthy Cat (Beginning)": "",
  "Last Stand of the Panthers (Beginning)": "",
  "Okita arrived and the thugs ran away, yet Okita says he doesn't know what I'm talking about. Was that... maybe not the real Okita? Impossible.": "",
  "Those thugs sure made themselves scarce once Okita showed up. Guess the place'll have some peace for the time being.": "",
  "That child who was in such a hurry at Kawaramachi... He was clearly worried about something. Seemed he was meeting up with a girl.": "",
  "That couple by Umekojicho over in Rakugai seemed to be in a stormy situation… Wonder if they're still fighting?": "",
  "The Dark Ebisu's been caught, but apparently he's not the same guy the old lady talked about. Could he have been the real... No, that's impossible.": "",
  "Why do I have to fight a bear!? The world is more dangerous than I thought!": "",
  "I gave the beggar some food. Who knows what'll come of that...": "",
  "He was a dangerous man, and he had great instincts. I'm sure he'll be even more formidable next time I see him...": "",
  "They need a cherry blossom tree to bury their dog, Kazukichi. I think I've seen a tree like that somewhere nearby... Where was it?": "",
  "Kanda wasn't so enthused, what with all the other guys spoiling the mood. He'd probably enjoy something a little different.": "",
  "They say that those who believe in this cat will be saved. Not sure I agree, but the cat's definitely a clever one.": "",
  "No way is it possible for a cat to bring good luck. Then again, this cat near the temple seems to get pretty lucky...": "",
  "Hirakawa fired most of the couriers after she saw Inamoto get beaten. Now, to release Hirakawa from the curse of being Kyo's Fastest, I just need to beat the last courier, Takeda.": "",
  "I hesitated telling the old man about the tree. It's so sad. Now I can only hope they'll eventually find happiness again. ...I'm sorry, folks.": "",
  "I didn't manage to see her face, but I did manage to protect her.": "",
  "Buyo is a pretty deep art form. Maybe it's time to visit Nichibuza again.": "",
  "I guess you do need to take care of your hips. I should help the udon shop when I have the time.": "",
  "You're one rotten bastard, Kurata. Don't expect mercy from me.": "",
  "Kurata's got a pretty intimidating guard at his mansion, so I should go in prepared... Maybe I could buy some stuff with the cash from Yae.": "",
  "The wood cutter hurt his back and seems to be in some trouble. Shouldn't I help him?": "",
  "I helped the wood cutter, but I think he's going to need more assistance for the time being.": "",
  "Looks like Fujie and the Tosa woman are going to keep up their letter-writing. So Fujie's going to need a Tosa tutor for a while yet!": "",
  "So Fujie's proposal was a success. Warms my heart to think that my knowledge of the Tosa dialect helped him out.": "",
  "Fujie went to Tosa to meet the person he's been writing to. He said he's going to propose! Hope that works out...": "",
  "I gave the stranger some food I made. He thought it was actually made by a loving wife...": "",
  "Sure, I had to talk to a stranger, but overall it seems nice to eat here. Just need to remember to bring my own food next time...": "",
  "A place where everyone can learn... Hard for me to imagine, but I'm sure Yae can make her dream a reality.": "",
  "I made a deal with a mysterious foreigner, and apparently we're going to continue on this path. Who is this man...?": "",
  "That mysterious foreigner asked me to bring ten tomatoes. Kind of a strange request, but I'd be paid handsomely...": "",
  "That woman who dropped her wallet said she really wanted some vegetables. It'd be nice to help her.": "",
  "I promised some vegetables to the woman who dropped her wallet.": "",
  "That man protected the tea store employee all by himself. He's clearly no ordinary man. And yet, I feel pity for him...": "",
  "Didn't think she'd dispatch the folks at the gambling den so easily. Spitfire through and through…": "",
  "There was a gang of thugs giving a guy a hard time over at the gambling den. I wonder if they're still at it?": "",
  "An innocent woman is being harassed. This won't be tolerated!": "",
  "The mother asked me to encourage her loner son to get out and be more social. Maybe if I have time I'll visit them in East Umekojicho.": "",
  "The courier isn't able to finish his deliveries. So, since I walk around the city a lot, I might as well help him out.": "",
  "The Captain and the Curious (Beginning)": "",
  "I promised to give the boy some vegetables. I could get some extra ones from the house...": "",
  "I'm glad things worked out between Oguri and Suzu. Physical appearance isn't always what attraction is all about.": "",
  "I wonder if Natsumi, the writer next door, managed to get his story down on paper?": "",
  "Did that writer next door, Natsumi, ever finish drafting his story? Hope he doesn't have writer's block.": "",
  "There's a man on the ground who hit his head. He needs help!": "",
  "I told the courier how to get to Fushimi Ichibangai. I wonder if he ever made it.": "",
  "What a horrible liquid that perfume turned out to be. If it ever becomes widespread in Japan, millions of men's lives will be ruined!": "",
  "Those wild guys were acting that way because of the times. It's not a good thing that so many people feel so restless these days... Can't deny the feeling in the air.": "",
  "Apparently there's a merchant selling perfume somewhere in Dead Man's Quarter. And I've got some extra money...": "",
  "What kind of job is \"the Brawler of Mukurogai\"?": "",
  "I think the Brawler of Mukurogai had more tattoos on his body...": "",
  "I heard a rumor about a fallen warrior who haunts swordsmen on the east side of Mukurogai. But he only appears at night...": "",
  "I met a fisherman who's never caught a fish. And if he doesn't catch one soon, he'll never cast a rod again. So I promised to bring him a fish!": "",
  "I gave a fish to the world's worst fisherman. I wonder if he ever managed to catch anything himself...": "",
  "Black ships... If they land at this pier, they'll cause absolute chaos.": "",
  "The man from the black ship got seasick and collapsed. He might be a foreign enemy—I need to ask him some questions! Maybe someone here knows how to cure seasickness.": "",
  "The man from the black ship went home with plenty of umeboshi. I hope some day it'll just be normal to interact with foreigners like him, but with everyone so distrustful, it may be a while!": "",
  "The Panthers' Leading Man (Beginning)": "",
  "Enter the Black Panther Couriers (Beginning)": "",
  "Hoshi, the raid captain of the Black Panthers, wants a rematch! He's probably waiting right now on Shijo Bridge. Wasn't his victory from last time enough for him?": "",
  "Makino, the leading man of the Black Panthers, wants to race again. Guess his first victory isn't good enough for him. He's probably somewhere near the Satsuma Consulate.": "",
  "Argh, I lost to Inamoto! I can't let this stand. Maybe I'll pay him a visit. He's probably on the bridge near the gambling den...": "",
  "Hirakawa's letter contained the location where my race with Inamoto was supposed to be. He's probably waiting on the bridge near the gambling den.": "",
  "I beat Hoshi of the Black Panthers, but it's clear that group isn't through with me yet. This can only lead to trouble.": "",
  "I defeated Makino of the Black Panthers, and immediately afterwards Inamoto challenged me. That's a guy who keeps calm and doesn't make mistakes, so this'll be a challenge.": "",
